{{also|Thwaite}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|*thwait}}, a borrowing from {{der|en|non|þveit|t=paddock}}. Compare {{cog|non|þveita|t=to hurl}} (see {{m|en|whittle}}), Danish {{m|da|døjt}} (“1/160 of the gulden”, dialectal: “a small coin”), German {{m|de|Deut}}, Dutch {{m|nl|duit}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|þwītan|t=to [[thwite]]; cut; cut off}}. {{doublet|en|doit}}, and possibly of ''{{l|en|twat}}''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/θweɪt/}}

